reference, or the Kaspa developers.

It holds no source file of the KCC20 reference, no file copied from its
repository and no line of the source text of its contracts. What in it
comes from the work of others:

1. Compiled contract scripts inside the recorded transactions.

   A Kaspa transaction that spends a coin of a contract reveals the
   contract's script. Of the 16 transactions kept in

     launch/results/2026-10-11-testnet-10/chain.json

   the 15 that spend a coin of a contract (all but the launch) therefore
   carry, in their signature scripts, compiled scripts of the contracts
   KCC20, PublicMint and TokenSeed of the KCC20 reference,
   https://github.com/argent-lang/kcc20-reference, revision c8a0871. They are
   the three compiled scripts whole: after the state fields of each coin,
   byte for byte the bytecode in that repository's
   fixtures/public-mint/artifact.json. The 13 accepted transactions were
   accepted by Kaspa testnet-10 nodes on 2026-10-11 and were public there;
   between them they reveal all three scripts. The 3 refused transactions
   kept beside them carry two of the three, KCC20 and TokenSeed. No other
   file of this repository carries them.

   The contracts are the work of the contributors of that repository, named
