3. Rules of a Kaspa node, ported, in engine/.

   The crate engine/crates/node-gate answers what a node would say about a
   transaction without running a node. The script engine and the mass
   calculator are the node's own packages, used as dependencies (see 5).
   The rules around them are ported, with changes, from rusty-kaspa,
   https://github.com/kaspanet/rusty-kaspa, revision
   a41a333b08848f41bf737b72592e463a6011b8ac, into these files:

     engine/crates/node-gate/src/isolation.rs
     engine/crates/node-gate/src/header.rs
     engine/crates/node-gate/src/utxo.rs
     engine/crates/node-gate/src/block.rs
     engine/crates/node-gate/src/policy.rs
     engine/crates/node-gate/src/mass.rs (two functions)

   One function of engine/crates/node-gate/src/engine.rs, parse, evaluates
   again the checks the engine makes on an opcode before it runs it
   (crypto/txscript/src/lib.rs, lines 622-629 and 656-669), with
   upstream's conditions and errors; the order of the steps in gate.rs
   follows the node's.

   Each ported function names its upstream file and lines and, except in
   policy.rs, keeps its upstream name; in policy.rs the four upstream
   functions are split into one function per rule under names of this
   crate, and the four composing functions keep theirs;
   engine/crates/node-gate/README.md lists them. The texts
   of the refusals in policy.rs and block.rs are upstream's, word for word;
   the prefix "non-standard: " in front of some of them is this crate's.
   Three test files replay rusty-kaspa's own unit tests against these
   ports, with upstream's transactions, byte vectors and expected results:

     engine/crates/checks/tests/review_consensus_isolation.rs
     engine/crates/checks/tests/review_consensus_utxo.rs
     engine/crates/checks/tests/review_policy_upstream_vectors.rs

   Among upstream's test vectors are two transactions that its test file
   says are taken from existing transactions, naming their ids. They are
   run here as upstream runs them, under mainnet parameters, and are only
   read, offline, as the input of a check: nothing in this repository was
   ever sent to mainnet. The formatter settings in
   engine/crates/node-gate/rustfmt.toml follow rusty-kaspa's as well.

