4. What in engine/ follows the KCC20 reference without being copied from
   it.

   The checks read the reference - its compiled artifact and the two
   descriptions beside it (manifest.json, kcc20.json), its generated
   SilverScript and its conformance vectors - from a clone the reader
   makes; none of these files is included. The file
   engine/data/rule-inventory.json gives, for every refusing opcode of the
   three compiled contracts, its byte offset, its opcode name and the line
   numbers of the reference's sources it comes from, with a description in
   this study's own words; it reproduces no source text and no bytecode.
   The scenarios of the honest transactions in
   engine/crates/kcc20-family/src/shapes.rs and their values (amounts,
   coin values, key seeds, the covenant id of the script-only profile)
   follow the reference's tests and examples; the code is written anew.
   The names and values of the scheme constants and of the state fields in
   engine/crates/kcc20-family/src/states.rs are those of the reference and
   of the KCC-20 specification, and a few short helpers there and in
   shapes.rs, witness.rs and keys.rs do what the reference's tests and
   examples do. The cases built from the conformance vectors in
   engine/crates/checks/tests/port_transfer.rs and review_ports_token.rs
   are put together as the reference's own conformance test puts them
   together; the code is written anew. A few digests and test values are
   written out in tests: the id, the sizes, the template hashes, the
   dispatch tags and the function signatures of the reference's artifact,
   a digest of its conformance vectors, two template hashes that
   SilverScript's own tests use, and values of the test vectors of the KCC
   specifications, https://github.com/kaspanet/kccs (CC0).

